6. OPTIMIZATION PRIORITY ORDER

   Priority 1 (Highest Impact, Lowest Cost):
   - RAM-cached token lookups (sub-50ms)[reference:27]
   - TCP connection keep-warm (150ms → 15ms)[reference:28]
   - Thread pinning / CPU affinity
   - Disable Python GC during market hours

   Priority 2 (Medium Impact):
   - Move hot path to Rust/PyO3 (10-100x speedup)[reference:29]
   - ZeroMQ for IPC (10-100x faster than HTTP)[reference:30]
   - QuestDB batch writes (4.3M rows/sec)
   - Pre-compute static data

   Priority 3 (High Impact, Requires Infrastructure):
   - Colocation (milliseconds → microseconds)[reference:31]
   - Kernel-bypass networking (DPDK)
   - FPGA acceleration (444 ns end-to-end)[reference:32]

